// fixture for comlint_extrapos.comt -- comlint's INPUT, never run
// directly (never registered in run_all.comt). Exercises the
// max-positional-arguments check: ep_noThen calls if() with a second
// positional instead of :then, the exact motivating case for this
// check (if()'s own signature declares one positional plus :then/
// :else keywords, so the second positional here is never evaluated at
// all -- confirmed against IfThenElseFunc::execute(), which only ever
// pulls stack_arg_post_eval(0) and the :then/:else keywords); ep_then
// is the same test written correctly, with :then, and must stay
// unflagged; ep_switch calls switch() the real way, with its
// dynamically-named :case keywords -- a call supplying any keyword is
// already outside what the positional-arity check validates, so this
// must stay unflagged regardless of how many :case pairs it carries;
// ep_open calls open() with two positionals (name and mode), both
// optional but nested ([filename [modestr]]) -- both must count
// toward the max, not just the outer bracket, so this bare case must
// also stay unflagged; ep_allow is a second missing-:then call
// overridden by a preceding comlint:allow line; ep_atOk calls at()
// the ordinary way (list, index) -- at()'s signature leads with a
// top-level alternation ("list|attrlist|compview"), which must count
// as ONE required slot (whichever alternative is supplied), not three
// (one per alternative); ep_allowTab is a third missing-:then call
// whose comlint:allow comment has a literal tab between "//" and the
// text instead of a space, exercised for the override.

sampleList=(1,2,3)

ep_noThen=if(1 2)

ep_then=if(1 :then 2 :else 3)

ep_switch=switch(1 :case1 10 :case2 20 :case3 30)

ep_open=open("/dev/null" "r")

ep_atOk=at(sampleList 0)

// comlint:allow -- deliberately missing :then, exercised for the override
ep_allow=if(1 2)

//	comlint:allow -- same, but a tab separates "//" from the text
ep_allowTab=if(1 2)
